 "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VdthsLEjNd8Pcm2UbHyrC9", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["backoff_retry", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379646, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VdthsLEjNd8Pcm2UbHyrC9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 384150, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), but the test expects banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), which rounds halves to the nearest even digit. The function's own description already said it used banker's rounding, so only the code was wrong.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Now 2.665 rounds to 2.66 and 2.675 to 2.68, as the test expects.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n\nThe advisory tool doesn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement itself. The fix is based on the test and the function's description.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0158W3E56coxkSihYXZsXWkQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UktkEhYLQ8L3kKMzpU6DUB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Up19iK1kyRCj7CG3itqnvB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Tj7ENUaGWcKcKo6V3GEzPj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Aoqf5qHDcx1JnofUcUdbJ4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017DYsHjxFBQepknbURhPAhT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0192wTH69AJb4YA25nDd4zah", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VdthsLEjNd8Pcm2UbHyrC9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN)", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (per FIN-212). `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring said ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), but the test expects banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), which rounds halves to the nearest even digit. The function's own description already said it used banker's rounding, so only the code was wrong.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Now 2.665 rounds to 2.66 and 2.675 to 2.68, as the test expects.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n\nThe advisory tool doesn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement itself. The fix is based on the test and the function's description.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}